  "worked_solution": "The power set of $T,$ denoted $P(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $\u2205.$\n\nSo, let's list all possible subsets of $T$ using a tree diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14095809/assets/1ef8e646081305399cddbf6908bd8415d908dab3e9bb0e371d68b33e62084774.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram, the subsets of $T$ are\n\n$$\n\u2205={},\\,{k},\\,{m},\\,{o},\\,{k,m},\\,{k,o},\\,{m,o},\\,{k,m,o}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(T)={\u2205,{k},{m},{o},{k,m},{k,o},{m,o},{k,m,o}}.\n$$",
